Brian D Ziebart, Andrew L Maas, J Andrew Bagnell, and Anind K Dey. 2008.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Maximum entropy inverse reinforcement learning.. In <em id="bib.bib107.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Aaai</em>, Vol. 8. Chicago, IL, USA, 1433–1438.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib108" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Ziegler et al<span id="bib.bib108.2" class="ltx_text">.</span> (2020)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Daniel M. Ziegler, Nisan Stiennon, Jeffrey Wu, Tom B. Brown, Alec Radford, Dario Amodei, Paul Christiano, and Geoffrey Irving. 2020.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Fine-Tuning Language Models from Human Preferences.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">arXiv:1909.08593 [cs.CL]

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p">[Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate]Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes: Technical Appendix</p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>DeliData Evaluation Metrics</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coarse Accuracy.</span>
A binary metric that equals <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> if the group’s final submission exactly matches the solution set (all vowel cards <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cup" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∪</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cup</annotation></semantics></math> all odd-number cards), and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.
<em id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> This captures whether the group fully solved the Wason task, providing a strict measure of success.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fine-Grained Accuracy.</span>
A score in increments of <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25</annotation></semantics></math>, where points are awarded for (i) turning a vowel, (ii) turning an odd number, (iii) not turning an even number, and (iv) not turning a consonant.
<em id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> This reflects partial correctness and gives credit for reasoning steps that align with the rule, even if the final submission is not fully correct.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Performance Gain.</span>
Defined as the difference between the average group-level accuracy at the final turn and the average initial accuracy of individual participants from their initial <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">individual solutions at the start of the collaborative dialogue</span>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Gain}=\frac{1}{|G|}\sum_{g\in G}\text{Acc}_{\text{final}}(g)-\frac{1}{|P|}\sum_{p\in P}\text{Acc}_{\text{initial}}(p)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Gain</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mtext>final</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mtext>initial</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Gain}=\frac{1}{|G|}\sum_{g\in G}\text{Acc}_{\text{final}}(g)-\frac{1}{|P|}\sum_{p\in P}\text{Acc}_{\text{initial}}(p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I1.i3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> Measures the benefit of collaboration and intervention relative to participants’ solo reasoning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Individual Change.</span>
For each participant <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, computed as <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{p}=\text{Acc}_{\text{final}}(p)-\text{Acc}_{\text{initial}}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mtext>final</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Acc</mtext><mtext>initial</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{p}=\text{Acc}_{\text{final}}(p)-\text{Acc}_{\text{initial}}(p)</annotation></semantics></math>.
<em id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> Shows how much each participant personally improved or declined, revealing heterogeneity in learning from the interaction.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Common Ground Convergence.</span>
The first turn <math id="A1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> at which the majority-supported set of cards stabilizes and remains unchanged for the rest of the dialogue.
<em id="A1.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> Captures how quickly the group reaches a shared consensus, highlighting efficiency of reasoning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Support Entropy.</span>
For each turn <math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the Shannon entropy of stance distributions:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{t}=-\sum_{c}p_{t}(c)\log p_{t}(c)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>c</mi></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}=-\sum_{c}p_{t}(c)\log p_{t}(c),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(c)</annotation></semantics></math> is the fraction of participants supporting card <math id="A1.I1.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
<em id="A1.I1.i6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> High entropy indicates diverse, unresolved opinions (exploration), while low entropy reflects convergence toward consensus.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Majority Stability.</span>
The Jaccard similarity between majority-supported sets at consecutive turns:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(A_{t},A_{t+1})=\frac{|A_{t}\cap A_{t+1}|}{|A_{t}\cup A_{t+1}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(A_{t},A_{t+1})=\frac{|A_{t}\cap A_{t+1}|}{|A_{t}\cup A_{t+1}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I1.i7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> Measures how stable group consensus is across turns, distinguishing flip-flopping from steady alignment.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Turn-to-Turn Effect.</span>
The <math id="A1.I1.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> distance between support distributions across consecutive turns:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t}=\sum_{c}|p_{t}(c)-p_{t+1}(c)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>c</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t}=\sum_{c}|p_{t}(c)-p_{t+1}(c)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I1.i8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> Quantifies the size of stance shifts per turn, showing how strongly an intervention or dialogue changes opinions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Participant Consistency.</span>
The Jaccard similarity of a participant’s supported set of cards across their own turns.
<em id="A1.I1.i9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> Indicates whether participants maintain a stable line of reasoning or frequently switch stances.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Change-of-Mind Rate.</span>
The fraction of participants who switch stance on at least one card between two consecutive turns:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{CMR}_{t}=\frac{|\{p:S_{t}(p)\neq S_{t-1}(p)\}|}{|P|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>CMR</mtext><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CMR}_{t}=\frac{|\{p:S_{t}(p)\neq S_{t-1}(p)\}|}{|P|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.I1.i10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> Captures direct responsiveness to interventions by measuring how often participants revise their positions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Consensus Realignment.</span>
The proportion of turns where the majority support shifts closer to the correct solution set after the intervention.
<em id="A1.I1.i11.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> Indicates whether interventions are not only changing opinions, but doing so in a direction that improves collective reasoning.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Weights Task Evaluation Metrics</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the dialogue models with the following metrics. Each metric captures a different facet of how common ground and reasoning quality evolve during interaction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Final Total:</span>
This is the total number of common ground propositions at the end of a dialogue.
<em id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> It shows how much shared knowledge the group accumulated overall, regardless of whether it was correct or incorrect.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accuracy Adjusted Total:</span>
This adjusts the final total by penalizing incorrect propositions.
<em id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> It measures not just how much knowledge was built, but how reliable that knowledge is, favoring dialogues with fewer errors.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error-Free Relations:</span>
This counts only the propositions that are correct, ignoring the incorrect ones.
<em id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> It provides a direct measure of how much accurate common ground was achieved.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accuracy-to-Quantity Ratio:</span>
This ratio compares the number of error-free propositions to the total propositions produced.
<em id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> It reflects the efficiency of communication—whether participants generated mostly correct contributions or mixed in many errors.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error-Weighted Growth:</span>
This measures the per-turn growth of common ground, weighted by accuracy.
<em id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> It evaluates how consistently the dialogue added useful knowledge over time, showing whether progress was stable or error-prone.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Incorrect Percentage:</span>
This is the fraction of propositions in the final common ground that are incorrect.
<em id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> It directly captures how much of the dialogue’s output is misleading or wrong, giving a sense of reliability at the end.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per-turn proposition counts.</span>
Let <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\{\text{equality},\text{inequality},\text{order}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>equality</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>inequality</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>order</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\{\text{equality},\text{inequality},\text{order}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the categories.
At dialogue turn <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}^{(c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}^{(c)}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of unique propositions in category <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}=\bigcup_{c\in\mathcal{C}}S_{t}^{(c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}=\bigcup_{c\in\mathcal{C}}S_{t}^{(c)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the per-turn counts are</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}^{(c)}=\lvert S_{t}^{(c)}\rvert,\qquad N_{t}=\lvert S_{t}\rvert=\sum_{c\in\mathcal{C}}N_{t}^{(c)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}^{(c)}=\lvert S_{t}^{(c)}\rvert,\qquad N_{t}=\lvert S_{t}\rvert=\sum_{c\in\mathcal{C}}N_{t}^{(c)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> This measures how much shared structure (common ground) has been accumulated by turn <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, both overall and by type. It rewards introducing <em id="A2.I2.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">new</em> agreed facts rather than repeating old ones.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cumulative (final) total.</span>
For a dialogue with <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> turns, the final cumulative size is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{final}}=N_{T},\qquad N_{\mathrm{final}}^{(c)}=N_{T}^{(c)}\ \ \text{for each }c\in\mathcal{C}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>final</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>final</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for each </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{final}}=N_{T},\qquad N_{\mathrm{final}}^{(c)}=N_{T}^{(c)}\ \ \text{for each }c\in\mathcal{C}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> This is the amount of common ground the group ends with. Bigger values indicate broader shared understanding at the end of the conversation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per-turn growth and average growth rate.</span>
Define growth at turn <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t}=N_{t}-N_{t-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t}=N_{t}-N_{t-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The average growth rate is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{G}=\frac{1}{T-1}\sum_{t=2}^{T}G_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{G}=\frac{1}{T-1}\sum_{t=2}^{T}G_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> Growth captures how quickly new common ground is formed. High average growth indicates steady progress rather than early bursts or stagnation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Normalized final total.</span>
Given a task-specific upper bound <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> on attainable propositions,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{N}_{\mathrm{final}}=\frac{N_{\mathrm{final}}}{N_{\max}}\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>final</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>final</mi></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{N}_{\mathrm{final}}=\frac{N_{\mathrm{final}}}{N_{\max}}\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> This rescales outcomes to a common <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> range, enabling comparison across tasks or settings with different ceilings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error rate at the end (incorrect percentage).</span>
Let <math id="A2.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{final}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>final</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{final}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the final proposition set and let <math id="A2.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{true}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>true</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{true}}</annotation></semantics></math> encode the ground truth. Define the set of incorrect final propositions</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}=\{\,s\in\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{final}}\ :\ s\text{ contradicts }\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{true}}\,\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>final</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> contradicts </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>true</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}=\{\,s\in\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{final}}\ :\ s\text{ contradicts }\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{true}}\,\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the incorrect percentage</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathrm{err}}=100\times\frac{\lvert\mathcal{E}\rvert}{\lvert\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{final}}\rvert}\ \ (\%)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>err</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>final</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>%</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{err}}=100\times\frac{\lvert\mathcal{E}\rvert}{\lvert\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{final}}\rvert}\ \ (\%).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> This quantifies how noisy the final common ground is. Lower values mean the shared beliefs align better with ground truth.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error-free relations.</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{ok}}=N_{\mathrm{final}}-\lvert\mathcal{E}\rvert." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ok</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>final</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{ok}}=N_{\mathrm{final}}-\lvert\mathcal{E}\rvert.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> This is the count of <em id="A2.I2.i6.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">useful</em> (correct) propositions left standing. It separates signal from noise in the final state.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accuracy-adjusted total.</span>
With a task-dependent scaling factor <math id="A2.I2.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., <math id="A2.I2.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1.5</annotation></semantics></math>),</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{adj}}=\alpha\,N_{\mathrm{final}}\left(1-\frac{p_{\mathrm{err}}}{100}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>adj</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>final</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>err</mi></msub><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{adj}}=\alpha\,N_{\mathrm{final}}\left(1-\frac{p_{\mathrm{err}}}{100}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> This rewards building large common ground while penalizing errors. Two systems with the same size get different credit if one is cleaner.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accuracy-to-quantity ratio.</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{A/Q}}=\frac{N_{\mathrm{ok}}^{\,2}}{N_{\mathrm{final}}}\quad(\text{with }R_{\mathrm{A/Q}}=0\text{ if }N_{\mathrm{final}}=0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>ok</mi><mn> 2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>final</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>final</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{A/Q}}=\frac{N_{\mathrm{ok}}^{\,2}}{N_{\mathrm{final}}}\quad(\text{with }R_{\mathrm{A/Q}}=0\text{ if }N_{\mathrm{final}}=0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> This favors high precision <em id="A2.I2.i8.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">and</em> non-trivial quantity: squaring <math id="A2.I2.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{ok}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ok</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{ok}}</annotation></semantics></math> rewards being both correct and substantial, while dividing by <math id="A2.I2.i8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{final}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>final</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{final}}</annotation></semantics></math> penalizes bloated, error-prone sets.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Error-weighted growth.</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\mathrm{ew}}=\overline{G}\left(1-\frac{p_{\mathrm{err}}}{100}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>ew</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>err</mi></msub><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\mathrm{ew}}=\overline{G}\left(1-\frac{p_{\mathrm{err}}}{100}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> Progress that comes with fewer errors counts more. It discounts apparent momentum that is built on mistaken beliefs.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per-model aggregation (means).</span>
Given multiple dialogues <math id="A2.I2.i10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1,\dots,D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1,\dots,D</annotation></semantics></math> for a model, any dialogue-level metric <math id="A2.I2.i10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> is averaged as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{M}=\frac{1}{D}\sum_{d=1}^{D}M^{(d)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{M}=\frac{1}{D}\sum_{d=1}^{D}M^{(d)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> This summarizes a model’s central tendency across conversations, smoothing idiosyncrasies of individual runs.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard error of the mean (SEM).</span>
Let <math id="A2.I2.i11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{M^{(d)}\}_{d=1}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M^{(d)}\}_{d=1}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be dialogue-level values and let <math id="A2.I2.i11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{turns}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>turns</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{turns}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the total number of turns aggregated for that model (when treating turns as independent trials). Then an SEM estimate is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SEM}(M)=\frac{\sqrt{\frac{1}{D-1}\sum_{d=1}^{D}\bigl(M^{(d)}-\overline{M}\bigr)^{2}}}{\sqrt{N_{\mathrm{turns}}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>SEM</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>turns</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SEM}(M)=\frac{\sqrt{\frac{1}{D-1}\sum_{d=1}^{D}\bigl(M^{(d)}-\overline{M}\bigr)^{2}}}{\sqrt{N_{\mathrm{turns}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.I2.i11.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i11.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(or <math id="A2.I2.i11.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{D}</annotation></semantics></math> in a dialogue-averaging view).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.I2.i11.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i11.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I2.i11.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intuition:</em> SEM indicates uncertainty around the model’s mean metric. Smaller SEM means more stable performance across the evidence pooled (dialogues/turns).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma 0 (Token-Level IPO Equivalence).</h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In a token-level MDP with deterministic transitions, the policy <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> trained using <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-Preference Optimization or IPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., 2024</a>)</cite> with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi=I(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi=I(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to an optimal maximum entropy policy: <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}|s_{t})=\frac{\exp(Q_{\theta}(s_{t},a_{t})/\beta)}{\sum_{a^{\prime}}\exp(Q_{\theta}(s_{t},a^{\prime})/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}|s_{t})=\frac{\exp(Q_{\theta}(s_{t},a_{t})/\beta)}{\sum_{a^{\prime}}\exp(Q_{\theta}(s_{t},a^{\prime})/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the soft Bellman equation: <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\theta}(s_{t},a_{t})=r_{\text{IPO}}(s_{t},a_{t})+\gamma\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}[V_{\theta}(s_{t+1})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">IPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\theta}(s_{t},a_{t})=r_{\text{IPO}}(s_{t},a_{t})+\gamma\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}[V_{\theta}(s_{t+1})]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity-mapping.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We consider a general non-decreasing function <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi:[0,1]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi:[0,1]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, a reference policy <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}\in\Delta^{\mathcal{X}}_{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}\in\Delta^{\mathcal{X}}_{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a real positive regularisation parameter <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\mathbb{R}^{\ast}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\mathbb{R}^{\ast}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. From <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, the <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-preference optimization objective (<math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>PO) is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho}\ \mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x),\ y^{\prime}\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}\left[\Psi\left(p^{\ast}(y\succ y^{\prime}\mid x)\right)\right]-\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\,\|\,\pi_{\text{ref}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi}\ \mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho}\ \mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x),\ y^{\prime}\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}\left[\Psi\left(p^{\ast}(y\succ y^{\prime}\mid x)\right)\right]-\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\,\|\,\pi_{\text{ref}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is the context distribution, <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the general preference distribution, <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reference policy, <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> is a general non-decreasing function and <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              Note: Throughout this proof, we use <math id="footnote8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> to consistently denote both the temperature parameter in the softmax policy and the KL divergence regularization strength. These two interpretations are mathematically equivalent in the maximum entropy RL framework. In some referenced works like <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, this parameter is denoted as <math id="footnote8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, but we maintain <math id="footnote8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> for consistency.</span></span></span> is the KL-divergence regularization strength (or the temperature parameter in max-entropy RL; <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib107" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ziebart et al., 2008</a>)</cite>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">In a token-level MDP formulation, we can reframe Eq. <a href="#A3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> in terms of states and actions, where each action represents a token choice and states capture context:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\rho,a\sim\pi(\cdot|s),a^{\prime}\sim\mu(\cdot|s)}[\Psi(p^{*}(a\succeq a^{\prime}|s))]-\beta D_{KL}(\pi||\pi_{\text{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>⪰</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\rho,a\sim\pi(\cdot|s),a^{\prime}\sim\mu(\cdot|s)}[\Psi(p^{*}(a\succeq a^{\prime}|s))]-\beta D_{KL}(\pi||\pi_{\text{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that for a particular choice of <math id="A3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> as the sigmoid-inverse function, the form of the optimal policy satisfying Eq. <a href="#A3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> in terms of the optimal soft-Q function follows directly from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>. Under this choice of <math id="A3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>, Eq. <a href="#A3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> simply maximizes the reward function in the general MaxEnt RL setting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib107" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ziebart et al., 2008</a>; <a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peng et al., 2019</a>)</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})=\frac{\exp\left(Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})/\beta\right)}{\sum_{a_{t}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\exp\left(Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t}^{\prime})/\beta\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})=\frac{\exp\left(Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})/\beta\right)}{\sum_{a_{t}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\exp\left(Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t}^{\prime})/\beta\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the general case—where <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> represents arbitrary non-decreasing function—the equivalence is non-trivial. Specifically, we will </span><span id="A3.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">only</span><span id="A3.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text"> consider the case where <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity-function, as originally formulated <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Let us begin with the original IPO loss:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{IPO}(\pi,D)=\mathbb{E}_{(y^{w},y^{l})\sim D}\left[\left(h_{\pi}(y^{w},y^{l})-\frac{\beta^{-1}}{2}\right)^{2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{IPO}(\pi,D)=\mathbb{E}_{(y^{w},y^{l})\sim D}\left[\left(h_{\pi}(y^{w},y^{l})-\frac{\beta^{-1}}{2}\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\pi}(y,y^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\pi}(y,y^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\pi}(y,y^{\prime})=\log\left(\frac{\pi(y)\pi_{ref}(y^{\prime})}{\pi(y^{\prime})\pi_{ref}(y)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\pi}(y,y^{\prime})=\log\left(\frac{\pi(y)\pi_{ref}(y^{\prime})}{\pi(y^{\prime})\pi_{ref}(y)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, while the structure of <math id="A3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\pi}(y,y^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\pi}(y,y^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> might be familiar to the reader as the implicit reward advantage <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024b</a>)</cite> (ignoring scaling terms like <math id="A3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>), this form does not directly provide us meaningful information of the advantage at the token-level. Therefore, let us first express the responses <math id="A3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of two arbitrary trajectories <math id="A3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\{s_{0}^{w},a_{0}^{w},...,s_{N-1}^{w},a_{N-1}^{w}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>w</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\{s_{0}^{w},a_{0}^{w},...,s_{N-1}^{w},a_{N-1}^{w}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\prime}=\{s_{0}^{l},a_{0}^{l},...,s_{M-1}^{l},a_{M-1}^{l}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\prime}=\{s_{0}^{l},a_{0}^{l},...,s_{M-1}^{l},a_{M-1}^{l}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, without considering any preference ranking between them. Now, for these complete trajectories, we can rewrite the log-likelihood ratio or the LHS of Eq. <a href="#A3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> as follows:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{\pi}(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{\pi}(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\frac{\pi(\tau^{w})\pi_{\text{ref}}(\tau^{l})}{\pi(\tau^{l})\pi_{\text{ref}}(\tau^{w})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\frac{\pi(\tau^{w})\pi_{\text{ref}}(\tau^{l})}{\pi(\tau^{l})\pi_{\text{ref}}(\tau^{w})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\frac{\prod_{t=0}^{N-1}\pi(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})\cdot\prod_{t=0}^{M-1}\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}{\prod_{t=0}^{M-1}\pi(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})\cdot\prod_{t=0}^{N-1}\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">⋅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\frac{\prod_{t=0}^{N-1}\pi(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})\cdot\prod_{t=0}^{M-1}\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}{\prod_{t=0}^{M-1}\pi(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})\cdot\prod_{t=0}^{N-1}\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\prod_{t=0}^{N-1}\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}\right)-\log\left(\prod_{t=0}^{M-1}\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\prod_{t=0}^{N-1}\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}\right)-\log\left(\prod_{t=0}^{M-1}\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}-\sum_{t=0}^{M-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}-\sum_{t=0}^{M-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">From <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>, we know that in the token-level MDP for the general max-entropy RL setting, the optimal policy <math id="A3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> under soft Q-learning satisfies:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})=\exp\left(\frac{Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})-V^{*}(s_{t})}{\beta}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})=\exp\left(\frac{Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})-V^{*}(s_{t})}{\beta}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal Q-function, <math id="A3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal value function, and <math id="A3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is the temperature parameter.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">This formulation also holds for policies optimal under Eq. <a href="#A3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> for the case with identity mapping <math id="A3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi=I(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi=I(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, since the optimal policy <math id="A3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of the reference policy takes a similar structure:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}(\tau\mid x)\propto\pi_{\text{ref}}(\tau\mid x)\exp\left(\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\prime}\sim\mu(\cdot\mid x)}[p(\tau\succ\tau^{\prime})]}{\beta}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≻</mo><mi>τ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}(\tau\mid x)\propto\pi_{\text{ref}}(\tau\mid x)\exp\left(\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\tau^{\prime}\sim\mu(\cdot\mid x)}[p(\tau\succ\tau^{\prime})]}{\beta}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our core insight here is to notice that unlike the standard token-level RLHF maximum-entropy objective where actions are sampled from the policy itself to compute the reward, the optimal policy in above equation (with <math id="A3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi=I(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi=I(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>) samples trajectories directly from the behavior policy, <math id="A3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, the structure of the optimal policy remains consistent for both these objectives and LLMs-as-policies can always be represented as a soft-Q function for some reward function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib100" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, where in this case the reward is the </span><span id="A3.p17.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">preference</span><span id="A3.p17.1.3" class="ltx_text"> over an alternate trajectory.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for the reference policy, we can express:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})=\exp\left(\frac{Q_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})-V_{\text{ref}}}{\beta}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}\mid s_{t})=\exp\left(\frac{Q_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})-V_{\text{ref}}}{\beta}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can log-linearize these two forms to derive:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p21" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\pi^{*}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\pi^{*}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})-V^{*}(s_{t})}{\beta}-\frac{Q_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})-V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t})}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})-V^{*}(s_{t})}{\beta}-\frac{Q_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})-V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t})}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}(Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})-Q_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})-V^{*}(s_{t})+V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}(Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})-Q_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})-V^{*}(s_{t})+V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the Bellman equation (Eq. 7) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>, for any arbitrary non-terminal step <math id="A3.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p23" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})=r(s_{t},a_{t})+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})+V^{*}(s_{t+1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})=r(s_{t},a_{t})+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})+V^{*}(s_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">And similarly, in the case of the reference model for <math id="A3.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p25" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})=r_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})+V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t+1})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})=r_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})+V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting these into our log-ratio:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p27" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\pi^{*}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\pi^{*}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}(r(s_{t},a_{t})+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})+V^{*}(s_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}(r(s_{t},a_{t})+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})+V^{*}(s_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-r_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})-\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})-V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-r_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})-\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})-V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-V^{*}(s_{t})+V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-V^{*}(s_{t})+V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}(r(s_{t},a_{t})-r_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})+V^{*}(s_{t+1})-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}(r(s_{t},a_{t})-r_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})+V^{*}(s_{t+1})-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t+1})-V^{*}(s_{t})+V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="1.000em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t+1})-V^{*}(s_{t})+V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since we want to express this in terms of the reward difference between the optimal and reference policies, we can define <math id="A3.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta r(s_{t},a_{t})=r(s_{t},a_{t})-r_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta r(s_{t},a_{t})=r(s_{t},a_{t})-r_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta V(s_{t})=V^{*}(s_{t})-V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta V(s_{t})=V^{*}(s_{t})-V_{\text{ref}}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives us:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p29" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\frac{\pi^{*}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\frac{\pi^{*}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}(\Delta r(s_{t},a_{t})+\Delta V(s_{t+1})-\Delta V(s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}(\Delta r(s_{t},a_{t})+\Delta V(s_{t+1})-\Delta V(s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a complete trajectory, summing over all token positions and using a telescopic series formulation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gunderson and Rosen, 2010</a>)</cite>, we find:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p31" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\pi^{*}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\pi^{*}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}(\Delta r(s_{t},a_{t})+\Delta V(s_{t+1})-\Delta V(s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}(\Delta r(s_{t},a_{t})+\Delta V(s_{t+1})-\Delta V(s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\Delta r(s_{t},a_{t})+\Delta V(s_{N})-\Delta V(s_{0})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\Delta r(s_{t},a_{t})+\Delta V(s_{N})-\Delta V(s_{0})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we can represent <math id="A3.p32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\pi}(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\pi}(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})</annotation></semantics></math> from Eq. <a href="#A3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> directly in terms policy log ratios to cumulative reward differences as follows:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p33" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{\pi}(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{\pi}(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}-\sum_{t=0}^{M-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{w}|s_{t}^{w})}-\sum_{t=0}^{M-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{l}|s_{t}^{l})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\Delta r(s_{t}^{w},a_{t}^{w})-\sum_{t=0}^{M-1}\Delta r(s_{t}^{l},a_{t}^{l})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\Delta r(s_{t}^{w},a_{t}^{w})-\sum_{t=0}^{M-1}\Delta r(s_{t}^{l},a_{t}^{l})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p34.1.1" class="ltx_text">The above result and the form of Eq. <a href="#A3.Ex29" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> shows that the optimal policy under IPO satisfies the soft Bellman equation:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\theta}(s_{t},a_{t})=r_{\text{IPO}}(s_{t},a_{t})+\gamma\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}[V_{\theta}(s_{t+1})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>IPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\theta}(s_{t},a_{t})=r_{\text{IPO}}(s_{t},a_{t})+\gamma\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}[V_{\theta}(s_{t+1})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p35" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p35.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{IPO}}(s_{t},a_{t})=r_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})+\Delta r(s_{t},a_{t})+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>IPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{IPO}}(s_{t},a_{t})=r_{\text{ref}}(s_{t},a_{t})+\Delta r(s_{t},a_{t})+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta r</annotation></semantics></math> represents the reward advantage over the reference policy—calibrated to achieve the target preference gap of <math id="A3.p35.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is the main result of our proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p36" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p36.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p36.1.1" class="ltx_text">Interestingly, this result aligns with Theorem 1 from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>, which establishes that all reward functions consistent with the same preference model induce equivalent policies when expressed in the form of Eq. <a href="#A3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>. </span><span id="A3.p36.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">More importantly, this result suggests the equivalence is satisfied not just for rewards that are optimal under the Bradley-Terry preference model </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A3.p36.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bradley and Terry, 1952</a><span id="A3.p36.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">)</span></cite><span id="A3.p36.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, but also for other equivalence classes of shaped rewards like </span><math id="A3.p36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{IPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">IPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{IPO}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.p36.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> that are derived directly from general preferences.</span><span id="A3.p36.1.8" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p37" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p37.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p37.1.1" class="ltx_text">To further derive the final form of the IPO loss, we can continue the argumentation from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and use an <math id="A3.p37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm-based approach to minimize the difference between this log-likelihood ratio and the target preference gap. As such, assuming we have access to preference annotated winning and losing trajectories (<math id="A3.p37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{l}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively) and sampling from the population preferences as a Bernoulli variable and preference symmetry <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Munos et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, we get:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p38" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{\text{IPO}}(\pi,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>IPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{\text{IPO}}(\pi,D)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})\sim D}\Bigg[\Bigg(h_{\pi}(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})-\frac{1}{2\beta}\Bigg)^{2}\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})\sim D}\Bigg[\Bigg(h_{\pi}(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})-\frac{1}{2\beta}\Bigg)^{2}\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})\sim D}\Bigg[\Bigg(\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{w}\mid s_{t}^{w})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{w}\mid s_{t}^{w})}-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})\sim D}\Bigg[\Bigg(\sum_{t=0}^{N-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{w}\mid s_{t}^{w})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{w}\mid s_{t}^{w})}-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\sum_{t=0}^{M-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{l}\mid s_{t}^{l})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{l}\mid s_{t}^{l})}-\frac{1}{2\beta}\Bigg)^{2}\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\sum_{t=0}^{M-1}\log\frac{\pi(a_{t}^{l}\mid s_{t}^{l})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}^{l}\mid s_{t}^{l})}-\frac{1}{2\beta}\Bigg)^{2}\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p39" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p39.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p39.1.1" class="ltx_text">This formulation directly corresponds to the IPO loss, where <math id="A3.p39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="A3.p39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> in the original paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., 2024</a>)</cite>) controls both the temperature in the policy and the strength of regularization toward the reference policy.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p40" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p40.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p40.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma 0 (Token-to-Intervention Bellman Completeness).</h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{t}=(S,A_{t},P_{t},r_{t},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{t}=(S,A_{t},P_{t},r_{t},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> be a token-level MDP and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{i}=(S,A_{i},P_{i},r_{i},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{i}=(S,A_{i},P_{i},r_{i},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> be the corresponding intervention-level MDP, where each action <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\in A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\in A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represents a complete friction intervention comprising a sequence of tokens <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=(a_{t}^{1},a_{t}^{2},\ldots,a_{t}^{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=(a_{t}^{1},a_{t}^{2},\ldots,a_{t}^{L})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assuming token-level Bellman completeness holds <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib87" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sutton and Barto, 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib105" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2024</a>)</cite> for function class <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., for any policy <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and any function <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f^{\prime}(s,a_{t})-T^{\pi}f(s,a_{t})\|_{\infty}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f^{\prime}(s,a_{t})-T^{\pi}f(s,a_{t})\|_{\infty}=0</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Bellman operator.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the optimal policy <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> derived via <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-preference optimization satisfies:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{I}(a_{i}|s)=\frac{\exp(Q^{I}(s,a_{i})/\beta)}{\sum_{a_{i}^{\prime}}\exp(Q^{I}(s,a_{i}^{\prime})/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{I}(a_{i}|s)=\frac{\exp(Q^{I}(s,a_{i})/\beta)}{\sum_{a_{i}^{\prime}}\exp(Q^{I}(s,a_{i}^{\prime})/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the intervention-level Bellman optimality equation.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p41" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p41.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p41.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under the token-level Bellman completeness assumption, for any state <math id="A3.p41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S</annotation></semantics></math> and intervention action <math id="A3.p41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\in A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\in A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> decomposed into <math id="A3.p41.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> tokens <math id="A3.p41.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=(a_{t}^{1},a_{t}^{2},\ldots,a_{t}^{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=(a_{t}^{1},a_{t}^{2},\ldots,a_{t}^{L})</annotation></semantics></math>, the approximation error of the value function is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p42" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{f^{\prime}\in\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{f^{\prime}\in\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|f^{\prime}(s,a_{i})-T_{i}^{\pi}f(s,a_{i})\|_{\infty}=\min_{f_{1},...,f_{L}\in\mathcal{F}}\|f_{1}(s,a_{i})-T_{t}^{\pi}f_{2}(s,a_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f^{\prime}(s,a_{i})-T_{i}^{\pi}f(s,a_{i})\|_{\infty}=\min_{f_{1},...,f_{L}\in\mathcal{F}}\|f_{1}(s,a_{i})-T_{t}^{\pi}f_{2}(s,a_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+r(s,a_{i})+\gamma^{1/L}\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P(\cdot|s,a_{i}),a_{t}^{1}\sim\pi(\cdot|s^{\prime})}[f_{2}(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+r(s,a_{i})+\gamma^{1/L}\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P(\cdot|s,a_{i}),a_{t}^{1}\sim\pi(\cdot|s^{\prime})}[f_{2}(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\gamma^{1/L}\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P(\cdot|s,a_{i}),a_{t}^{1}\sim\pi(\cdot|s^{\prime})}[T_{t}^{\pi}f_{3}(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1})]+\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\gamma^{1/L}\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P(\cdot|s,a_{i}),a_{t}^{1}\sim\pi(\cdot|s^{\prime})}[T_{t}^{\pi}f_{3}(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1})]+\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\gamma^{(L-1)/L}\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P(\cdot|s,a_{i}),a_{t}^{1:L-1}\sim\pi(\cdot|s^{\prime})}[f_{L}(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1:L-1})]-r(s,a_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\gamma^{(L-1)/L}\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P(\cdot|s,a_{i}),a_{t}^{1:L-1}\sim\pi(\cdot|s^{\prime})}[f_{L}(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1:L-1})]-r(s,a_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\gamma^{(L-1)/L}\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P(\cdot|s,a_{i}),a_{t}^{1:L-1}\sim\pi(\cdot|s^{\prime})}[T_{t}^{\pi}f(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1:L-1})]\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\gamma^{(L-1)/L}\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P(\cdot|s,a_{i}),a_{t}^{1:L-1}\sim\pi(\cdot|s^{\prime})}[T_{t}^{\pi}f(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1:L-1})]\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\min_{f_{1},...,f_{L}\in\mathcal{F}}\|f_{1}(s,a_{i})-T_{t}^{\pi}f_{2}(s,a_{i})\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\min_{f_{1},...,f_{L}\in\mathcal{F}}\|f_{1}(s,a_{i})-T_{t}^{\pi}f_{2}(s,a_{i})\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{i=2}^{L}\gamma^{(i-1)/L}\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P(\cdot|s,a_{i}),a_{t}^{1:i-1}\sim\pi(\cdot|s^{\prime})}[\|f_{i}(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1:i-1})-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{i=2}^{L}\gamma^{(i-1)/L}\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P(\cdot|s,a_{i}),a_{t}^{1:i-1}\sim\pi(\cdot|s^{\prime})}[\|f_{i}(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1:i-1})-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad T_{t}^{\pi}f(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1:i-1})\|_{\infty}]\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad T_{t}^{\pi}f(s^{\prime},a_{t}^{1:i-1})\|_{\infty}]\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p43" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p43.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p43.1.1" class="ltx_text">The last inequality follows from token-level Bellman completeness, which guarantees that for each component function, there exists an element in <math id="A3.p43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> that perfectly represents the Bellman update.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p44" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p44.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p44.1.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that intervention-level Bellman completeness holds, and therefore when <math id="A3.p44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-preference optimization is applied at the token level, the resulting policy can be expressed as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p45" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(25)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{I}(a_{i}|s)=\frac{\exp(Q^{I}(s,a_{i})/\beta)}{\sum_{a_{i}^{\prime}}\exp(Q^{I}(s,a_{i}^{\prime})/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{I}(a_{i}|s)=\frac{\exp(Q^{I}(s,a_{i})/\beta)}{\sum_{a_{i}^{\prime}}\exp(Q^{I}(s,a_{i}^{\prime})/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p46" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p46.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p46.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the </span><span id="A3.p46.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">intervention-level</span><span id="A3.p46.1.3" class="ltx_text"> Bellman optimality equation, which completes our proof. This result is crucial for our analysis of <math id="A3.p46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-Preference Optimization (<a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Ψ-Preference Optimization in Collaborative MAMDPs). ‣ Theoretical Insights. ‣ 3.1. Modeling Collaborative Problem Solving with Modified-Action MDPs ‣ 3. Background and Task Formulation ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) and DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024b</a>)</cite> (<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 0 (DPO Bellman Optimality in MAMDPs). ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), as it establishes that the soft Q-functions derived from these preference-alignment algorithms at the </span><span id="A3.p46.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">token</span><span id="A3.p46.1.5" class="ltx_text"> level maintain their optimality properties at the </span><span id="A3.p46.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">intervention</span><span id="A3.p46.1.7" class="ltx_text"> level. This is particularly important in our collaborative MAMDP setting, where both the friction and collaborator agents operate on complete interventions as the standard linguistic unit. Operationally, this allows us to use intervention-level utility or reward measurements for quantifying the quality of friction interventions and their modifications.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p47" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p47.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p47.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Theorem 3 (<math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-Preference Optimization in Collaborative MAMDPs).</h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi:[0,1]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi:[0,1]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be any non-decreasing function and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a temperature parameter. Any intervention agent policy <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> trained via <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-preference optimization with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> as identity-mapping in a collaborative MAMDP <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{f}=(\mathcal{M},P_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{f}=(\mathcal{M},P_{A})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}(a|s,\pi^{I})=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\cdot\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}(a|s,\pi^{I})=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\cdot\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> represents modifications by a collaborator policy <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(26)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{I}(a|s)=\frac{\exp(Q^{I}(s,a)/\beta)}{\sum_{a^{\prime}}\exp(Q^{I}(s,a^{\prime})/\beta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{I}(a|s)=\frac{\exp(Q^{I}(s,a)/\beta)}{\sum_{a^{\prime}}\exp(Q^{I}(s,a^{\prime})/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the Bellman optimality equation for the underlying MDP <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, disregarding the collaborator’s modifications through <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p48" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p48.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p48.1.1" class="ltx_text">From <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 0 (Token-Level IPO Equivalence). ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we know that a policy trained using <math id="A3.p48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-Preference Optimization with Identity mapping in a token-level MDP corresponds to an optimal maximum entropy policy expressible via soft Q-learning. We now extend this result to the collaborative MAMDP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Langlois and Everitt, 2021</a>)</cite> setting.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p49" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p49.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p49.1.1" class="ltx_text">The general <math id="A3.p49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>-preference optimization objective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., 2024</a>)</cite> is originally defined over responses <math id="A3.p49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p49.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(27)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho,y\sim\pi(\cdot|x),y^{\prime}\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}[\Psi(p^{*}(y\succ y^{\prime}|x))]-\beta D_{KL}(\pi||\pi_{\text{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\rho,y\sim\pi(\cdot|x),y^{\prime}\sim\mu(\cdot|x)}[\Psi(p^{*}(y\succ y^{\prime}|x))]-\beta D_{KL}(\pi||\pi_{\text{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p50" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p50.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p50.1.1" class="ltx_text">In our token-level MDP formulation, we can reframe this in terms of states and actions, where each action represents a token choice and states capture context:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(28)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi^{F}}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\rho,a\sim\pi^{F}(\cdot|s),a^{\prime}\sim\mu(\cdot|s)}[\Psi(p^{*}(a\succeq a^{\prime}|s))]-\beta D_{KL}(\pi^{I}||\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>F</mi></msup></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>⪰</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi^{F}}\mathbb{E}_{s\sim\rho,a\sim\pi^{F}(\cdot|s),a^{\prime}\sim\mu(\cdot|s)}[\Psi(p^{*}(a\succeq a^{\prime}|s))]-\beta D_{KL}(\pi^{I}||\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p51" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p51.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p51.1.1" class="ltx_text">From <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 0 (Token-Level IPO Equivalence). ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, in a token-level MDP where <math id="A3.p51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity mapping, the corresponding soft Q-learning policy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib100" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025</a>)</cite> takes the following form:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(29)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{I}(s,a)=r_{\Psi}(s,a)+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I}(a|s)+\gamma\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}}\left[\max_{a^{\prime}}Q^{I}(s^{\prime},a^{\prime})\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext><mi>I</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{I}(s,a)=r_{\Psi}(s,a)+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I}(a|s)+\gamma\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}}\left[\max_{a^{\prime}}Q^{I}(s^{\prime},a^{\prime})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p51.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p51.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\Psi}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\Psi}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the reward function under the identity mapping. Now, from Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 0 (Token-to-Intervention Bellman Completeness). ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we know that under the assumption of token-level Bellman completeness, a policy trained via token-level preference optimization preserves optimality properties when extended to </span><span id="A3.p51.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">intervention</span><span id="A3.p51.2.3" class="ltx_text">-level or complete friction interventions. This aligns with findings by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib100" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025)</a></cite>, who demonstrated that when policies are parameterized by logits, grouping tokens into macro-actions preserves both sequence probability and policy structure. </span><span id="A3.p51.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">This theoretical foundation is crucial in our MAMDP setting because it allows us to analyze and measure the quality of the friction agent’s policy at the intervention level while training occurs token-by-token.</span><span id="A3.p51.2.5" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p52" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p52.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p52.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, let us consider the MAMDP action modification function <math id="A3.p52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, which transforms intended actions according to the collaborator policy <math id="A3.p52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Refer <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Example 0 (Action Modification in DeliData Wason Card Task). ‣ 3.1. Modeling Collaborative Problem Solving with Modified-Action MDPs ‣ 3. Background and Task Formulation ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for an intuitive example of this modification.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p53" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(30)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{A}(a|s,\pi^{I})=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\cdot\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{A}(a|s,\pi^{I})=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\cdot\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p54" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p54.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p54.1.1" class="ltx_text">The empirical policy affecting the environment is therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(31)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\pi}^{I}(a|s)=P_{A}(a|s,\pi^{I})=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\cdot\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\pi}^{I}(a|s)=P_{A}(a|s,\pi^{I})=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\cdot\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p55" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p55.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p55.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the empirical policy <math id="A3.p55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\pi}^{I}(a|s)=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\cdot\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\pi}^{I}(a|s)=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\cdot\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, we verify it forms a valid probability distribution. Assuming both <math id="A3.p55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>F</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p55.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> are valid probability distributions, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p56" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{a\in A}\dot{\pi}^{I}(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{a\in A}\dot{\pi}^{I}(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in A}\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a\in A}\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\sum_{a\in A}\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\sum_{a\in A}\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p56.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p56.1.1" class="ltx_text">where we use <math id="A3.p56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a\in A}\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a\in A}\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.p56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,a^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,a^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p56.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.p56.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p57" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p57.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p57.1.1" class="ltx_text">However, weight updates on <math id="A3.p57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="A3.p57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{IPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>IPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{IPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> depends solely on trajectory preferences without accounting for these modifications. The gradient updates to the policy parameters directly optimize the virtual policy <math id="A3.p57.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, not the empirical policy <math id="A3.p57.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\pi}^{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>F</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\pi}^{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p58" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p58.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p58.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Bellman updates never incorporate <math id="A3.p58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.p58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the policy optimizes:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(32)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{I}(s)=\arg\max_{a}Q^{I}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>a</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{I}(s)=\arg\max_{a}Q^{I}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p59" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p59.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p59.1.1" class="ltx_text">which satisfies the Bellman optimality equation for <math id="A3.p59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> regardless of the collaborator’s modifications.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p60" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p60.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p60.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Everitt et al., 2021a</a>)</cite>, <math id="A3.p60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimal for the underlying MDP <math id="A3.p60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> while being completely unaware of how its actions are modified by the collaborator through <math id="A3.p60.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Proposition 0 (DPO Bellman Optimality in MAMDPs).</h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A friction agent policy <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> trained via DPO in a collaborative MAMDP <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{f}=(\mathcal{M},P_{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{f}=(\mathcal{M},P_{A})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the Bellman optimality objective for the underlying MDP <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby ignoring the effect of the collaborator’s action modifications <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p61" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p61.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p61.1.1" class="ltx_text">We define the collaborative MAMDP where <math id="A3.p61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the collaborator policy <math id="A3.p61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{C}</annotation></semantics></math> that modifies friction interventions:
<math id="A3.p61.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}(a|s,\pi^{I})=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\cdot\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}(a|s,\pi^{I})=\sum_{a^{\prime}\in A}\pi^{I}(a^{\prime}|s)\cdot\pi^{C}(a|s,a^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p62" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p62.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p62.1.1" class="ltx_text">The DPO objective optimizes the friction policy by minimizing:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\pi_{\theta}^{I},\mathcal{D})=-\mathbb{E}_{(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{I}(\tau^{w})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I}(\tau^{w})}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{I}(\tau^{l})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I}(\tau^{l})}\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\pi_{\theta}^{I},\mathcal{D})=-\mathbb{E}_{(\tau^{w},\tau^{l})\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{I}(\tau^{w})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I}(\tau^{w})}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}^{I}(\tau^{l})}{\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I}(\tau^{l})}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p62.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p62.2.1" class="ltx_text">This optimization yields a policy expressible as a softmax over action values:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}^{I}(a|s)=\frac{\exp(Q_{\theta}^{I}(s,a)/\beta)}{\sum_{a^{\prime}}\exp(Q_{\theta}^{I}(s,a^{\prime})/\beta)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}^{I}(a|s)=\frac{\exp(Q_{\theta}^{I}(s,a)/\beta)}{\sum_{a^{\prime}}\exp(Q_{\theta}^{I}(s,a^{\prime})/\beta)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p62.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p62.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\theta}^{I}(s,a)=\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I}(a|s)+r_{\text{pref}}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext><mi>I</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\theta}^{I}(s,a)=\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I}(a|s)+r_{\text{pref}}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p63" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p63.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p63.1.1" class="ltx_text">The DPO updates implicitly train these Q-values to satisfy:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\theta}^{I}(s,a)=r_{\text{DPO}}(s,a)+\gamma\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P_{S}(s,a)}\left[\max_{a^{\prime}}Q_{\theta}^{I}(s^{\prime},a^{\prime})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>I</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\theta}^{I}(s,a)=r_{\text{DPO}}(s,a)+\gamma\mathbb{E}_{s^{\prime}\sim P_{S}(s,a)}\left[\max_{a^{\prime}}Q_{\theta}^{I}(s^{\prime},a^{\prime})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p63.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p63.2.1" class="ltx_text">This update rule corresponds exactly to the Bellman optimality equation for <math id="A3.p63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> with reward function <math id="A3.p63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{DPO}}(s,a)=r_{\text{pref}}(s,a)+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I}(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext><mi>I</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{DPO}}(s,a)=r_{\text{pref}}(s,a)+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}^{I}(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p64" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p64.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p64.1.1" class="ltx_text">Critically, the DPO optimization process never incorporates <math id="A3.p64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.p64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Q-value updates do not account for the friction agent’s chosen action <math id="A3.p64.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> being potentially transformed into <math id="A3.p64.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{a}\sim\pi^{C}(\cdot|s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\sim\pi^{C}(\cdot|s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>. While the empirical policy affecting the environment is <math id="A3.p64.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\pi}^{I}(a|s)=P_{A}(a|s,\pi^{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>I</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\pi}^{I}(a|s)=P_{A}(a|s,\pi^{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, the DPO updates are based solely on the virtual policy <math id="A3.p64.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p65" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p65.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p65.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Proposition 2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Everitt et al. (2021a)</a></cite>, policies satisfying the Bellman optimality objective for a MAMDP are optimal for the underlying MDP regardless of action modifications. Therefore, <math id="A3.p65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{I}</annotation></semantics></math> trained via DPO optimizes for <math id="A3.p65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> while ignoring the collaborator’s modifications through <math id="A3.p65.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma 0 (Token-Level Q-function Equivalence).</h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In a token-level MDP with deterministic transitions, the LLM logits <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> trained using DPO represent an optimal Q-function <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{*}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{*}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to some reward function <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p66" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p66.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p66.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the Bellman equation in the token-level MDP:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(33)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r(s_{t},a_{t})+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})+V^{*}(s_{t+1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r(s_{t},a_{t})+\beta\log\pi_{\text{ref}}(a_{t}|s_{t})+V^{*}(s_{t+1}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p66.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p66.2.1" class="ltx_text">The optimal policy is then related to <math id="A3.p66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> via:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(34)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi^{*}(a_{t}|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi^{*}(a_{t}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{(Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})-V^{*}(s_{t}))/\beta}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{(Q^{*}(s_{t},a_{t})-V^{*}(s_{t}))/\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p66.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p66.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since this corresponds to a softmax over logits <math id="A3.p66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> with temperature <math id="A3.p66.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, and because DPO optimizes these logits to match preference data, it follows that DPO effectively learns a Q-function representation.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1. </span>Proof of Optimal Friction Intervention Policy</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The structure of this solution follows standard results in RL and control theory literature, appearing in preference alignment frameworks for LLMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib107" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ziebart et al., 2008</a>; <a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peng et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and CoT-based alignment frameworks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Choi et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. We simply demonstrate that a similar application holds for <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeauthor"><a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nath et al.</a></cite>’s FAAF model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nath et al., 2025a</a>)</cite> in our collaborative setting where <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">intervention agent</span> is additionally conditioned on the frictive state, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. This proof follows similar reasoning as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al. (2024)</a></cite>. Let us recall the general preference optimization objective for <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">intervention agent</span> in Eq. <a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ Training. ‣ 3.3. How Do We Train An Intervention Agent? ‣ 3. Background and Task Formulation ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, assuming <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> as identity-mapping <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(35)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}^{*}_{\text{FAAF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒥</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">FAAF</mtext><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}^{*}_{\text{FAAF}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\min_{\pi^{\prime}}\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}x\sim\rho\\
\phi\sim\pi^{\prime}(\cdot\mid x)\\
f\sim\pi(\cdot\mid\phi,x)\end{subarray}}\Bigg[\mathcal{P}(f\succ f^{\prime}\mid\phi,x)-\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}\mid\phi,x)+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></munder><munder><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi></munder><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒫</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≻</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϕ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min_{\pi^{\prime}}\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}x\sim\rho\\
\phi\sim\pi^{\prime}(\cdot\mid x)\\
f\sim\pi(\cdot\mid\phi,x)\end{subarray}}\Bigg[\mathcal{P}(f\succ f^{\prime}\mid\phi,x)-\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}\mid\phi,x)+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{\prime}\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}\mid x)\Bigg]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">π</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi^{\prime}\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}\mid x)\Bigg].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For fixed <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the inner maximization reduces to the regularized objective:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(36)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\beta}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\beta}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E36.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{f\sim\pi}[\mathcal{P}(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x)]-\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}|\phi,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{f\sim\pi}[\mathcal{P}(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x)]-\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}|\phi,x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{f}\pi(f|\phi,x)\mathcal{P}(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x)-\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}|\phi,x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>f</mi></munder></mstyle><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{f}\pi(f|\phi,x)\mathcal{P}(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x)-\beta D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}|\phi,x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> comes from a finite space of friction <span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">interventions</span>, <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x)</annotation></semantics></math> provides the preference feedback from collaborator participants, <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly positive, and <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi,\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi,\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> are LLM policies. Note that <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(f|\phi,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(f|\phi,x)</annotation></semantics></math> is a valid probability distribution, satisfying:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(37)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{f}\pi(f|\phi,x)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>f</mi></munder><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{f}\pi(f|\phi,x)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Let us first define the optimal friction intervention policy <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="A3.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(38)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}(f|\phi,x)=\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f|\phi,x)\exp(\beta^{-1}p(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x))}{Z^{*}(\phi,x)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}(f|\phi,x)=\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f|\phi,x)\exp(\beta^{-1}p(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x))}{Z^{*}(\phi,x)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{*}(\phi,x)=\sum_{f^{\prime}}\pi_{\text{ref}}(f^{\prime}|\phi,x)\exp(\beta^{-1}p(f^{\prime}\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{*}(\phi,x)=\sum_{f^{\prime}}\pi_{\text{ref}}(f^{\prime}|\phi,x)\exp(\beta^{-1}p(f^{\prime}\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x))</annotation></semantics></math>. Under these definitions:</p>
<table id="A3.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(39)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}=\underset{\pi}{\operatorname{arg\,max}}\mathcal{L}_{\beta}(\pi)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝜋</mo></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}=\underset{\pi}{\operatorname{arg\,max}}\mathcal{L}_{\beta}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(40)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathcal{L}_{\beta}(\pi)}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathcal{L}_{\beta}(\pi)}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E40.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\pi(f|\phi,x)\frac{p(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x)}{\beta}-D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}|\phi,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\pi(f|\phi,x)\frac{p(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x)}{\beta}-D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi_{\text{ref}}|\phi,x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\pi(f|\phi,x)\big(\frac{p(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x)}{\beta}-\log\big(\frac{\pi(f|\phi,x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f|\phi,x)}\big)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\pi(f|\phi,x)\big(\frac{p(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x)}{\beta}-\log\big(\frac{\pi(f|\phi,x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f|\phi,x)}\big)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\pi(f|\phi,x)\log\big(\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f|\phi,x)\exp(\beta^{-1}p(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x))}{\pi(f|\phi,x)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\pi(f|\phi,x)\log\big(\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f|\phi,x)\exp(\beta^{-1}p(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x))}{\pi(f|\phi,x)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\pi(f|\phi,x)\log\big(\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f|\phi,x)\exp(\beta^{-1}p(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x))}{Z^{*}(\phi,x)}\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em">⋅</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\pi(f|\phi,x)\log\big(\frac{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f|\phi,x)\exp(\beta^{-1}p(f\succ f^{\prime}|\phi,x))}{Z^{*}(\phi,x)}\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(41)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{Z^{*}(\phi,x)}{\pi(f|\phi,x)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{Z^{*}(\phi,x)}{\pi(f|\phi,x)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\pi(f|\phi,x)\log\big(\frac{\pi^{*}(f|\phi,x)}{\pi(f|\phi,x)}\big)+\log Z^{*}(\phi,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{f\in\mathcal{F}}\pi(f|\phi,x)\log\big(\frac{\pi^{*}(f|\phi,x)}{\pi(f|\phi,x)}\big)+\log Z^{*}(\phi,x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi^{*})+\log Z^{*}(\phi,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi^{*})+\log Z^{*}(\phi,x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{*}=\underset{\pi}{\operatorname{arg\,max}}\big[-D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi^{*})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝜋</mo></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}=\underset{\pi}{\operatorname{arg\,max}}\big[-D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi^{*})\big]</annotation></semantics></math>. Since:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(42)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi^{*})=\frac{\mathcal{L}_{\beta}(\pi)}{\beta}-\log Z^{*}(\phi,x)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi^{*})=\frac{\mathcal{L}_{\beta}(\pi)}{\beta}-\log Z^{*}(\phi,x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log Z^{*}(\phi,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log Z^{*}(\phi,x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the partition function independent of <math id="A3.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the argmax of <math id="A3.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-D_{\text{KL}}(\pi\parallel\pi^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with that of <math id="A3.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\beta}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\beta}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Lemma 0 (Vanishing Gradient of Frictive State <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>).</h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{friction}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">friction</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{friction}}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ Training. ‣ 3.3. How Do We Train An Intervention Agent? ‣ 3. Background and Task Formulation ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), the direct contribution of the frictive state <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> to the gradient vanishes when the conditional probability is decomposed.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The gradient of the IPO-like <math id="A3.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{friction}}(\pi_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>friction</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{friction}}(\pi_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A3.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{friction}}(\pi_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>friction</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{friction}}(\pi_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}\bigg[2\delta\cdot\Big(\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|s,\phi)-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}\bigg[2\delta\cdot\Big(\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|s,\phi)-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(43)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\quad\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|s,\phi)\Big)\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\quad\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|s,\phi)\Big)\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(s,\phi,f_{w},f_{l})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(s,\phi,f_{w},f_{l})\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the preference dataset, <math id="A3.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|s,\phi)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{w}|s,\phi)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|s,\phi)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{l}|s,\phi)}-\frac{1}{2\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|s,\phi)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{w}|s,\phi)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|s,\phi)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{l}|s,\phi)}-\frac{1}{2\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,\phi,f_{w},f_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,\phi,f_{w},f_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the context, frictive state, winning and losing friction interventions, respectively.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Decomposing the conditional distribution in a standard fashion:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(44)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\pi_{\theta}(f|s,\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\pi_{\theta}(f|s,\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\pi_{\theta}(f,\phi|s)-\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\pi_{\theta}(f,\phi|s)-\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the gradient and applying the linearity of the gradient operator, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(45)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f|s,\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f|s,\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f,\phi|s)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f,\phi|s)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">The difference of gradients in the objective becomes:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(46)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|s,\phi)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|s,\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|s,\phi)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|s,\phi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w},\phi|s)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|s)-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w},\phi|s)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|s)-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l},\phi|s)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|s)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l},\phi|s)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|s)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w},\phi|s)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l},\phi|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w},\phi|s)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l},\phi|s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the <math id="A3.SS1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|s)</annotation></semantics></math> terms cancel out, showing that the direct contribution of <math id="A3.SS1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes in the gradient computation. Note that <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pal et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib102" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> provides a similar argument to empirically show that DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>’s loss suffers from a similar vanishing gradient problem limiting policy learning especially when the preferred and the dispreferred responses or CoT-</span><span id="A3.SS1.p16.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">trajectories</span><span id="A3.SS1.p16.1.3" class="ltx_text"> are highly similar at the string level. These studies show </span><span id="A3.SS1.p16.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">when</span><span id="A3.SS1.p16.1.5" class="ltx_text"> DPO might assign low likelihood to the winning responses, despite the DPO implicit reward margin increasing during training. Subsequently <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024a</a>)</cite> offers theoretical justification for this phenomenon (reduction in the preferred response likelihood) with the additional insight that this is more likely when the policy first undergoes supervised-finetuning (SFT) and that this is expected from the perspective of the objective (MaxEnt RL in token-MDP)—with similar results seen also in the case of the general MDP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hejna et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. In contrast, our work extends this observation where additional random variables like frictive states <math id="A3.SS1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> are modeled as a part of the state decomposition in the token-MDP. As such, we extend this observation to learning algorithms like IPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al., 2024</a>)</cite> that optimize for general preferences.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Corollary 0.</h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The combined loss function <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}[(1/2\beta-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime}))^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">pref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}[(1/2\beta-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime}))^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> incorporating both conditional and marginal terms promotes more effective learning of the friction state gradient compared to the standard friction-IPO loss.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">To recall from <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3. How Do We Train An Intervention Agent? ‣ 3. Background and Task Formulation ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, our collaborative roleplay results in <math id="A3.SS1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}</annotation></semantics></math>—a dataset of tuples <math id="A3.SS1.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,\phi,f_{w},f_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,\phi,f_{w},f_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.SS1.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> represents context, <math id="A3.SS1.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is a frictive state, and <math id="A3.SS1.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{w},f_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{w},f_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> are preferred and non-preferred friction interventions, respectively. For simplicity we avoid notating the dialogue index <math id="A3.SS1.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and step <math id="A3.SS1.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider a flattened binary preference dataset of these tuples. Additionally, let <math id="A3.SS1.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nath et al. (2025a)</a></cite>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(47)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta R</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|\phi,s)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{w}|\phi,s)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|\phi,s)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{l}|\phi,s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|\phi,s)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{w}|\phi,s)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|\phi,s)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{l}|\phi,s)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(48)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|s)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{w}|s)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|s)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{l}|s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|s)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{w}|s)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|s)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{l}|s)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Starting with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citeauthor"><a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nath et al.</a></cite>’s loss function <math id="A3.SS1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{FAAF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>FAAF</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{FAAF}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nath et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(49)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">and then taking the gradient with respect to <math id="A3.SS1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(50)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[\nabla_{\theta}\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[2\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[2\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[2\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)\cdot\left(-\nabla_{\theta}(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[2\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)\cdot\left(-\nabla_{\theta}(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[-2\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)\cdot\nabla_{\theta}(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[-2\left(\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right)\cdot\nabla_{\theta}(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">We define <math id="A3.SS1.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}=\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}=\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for clarity:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(51)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E51.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[-2\delta^{\prime}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[-2\delta^{\prime}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[-2\delta^{\prime}\cdot(\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R+\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>pref</mtext></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\text{pref}}}\left[-2\delta^{\prime}\cdot(\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R+\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Expanding the terms <math id="A3.SS1.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A3.SS1.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 0 (Vanishing Gradient of Frictive State ϕ). ‣ C.1. Proof of Optimal Friction Intervention Policy ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(52)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|\phi,x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{w}|\phi,x)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|\phi,x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{l}|\phi,x)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|\phi,x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{w}|\phi,x)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|\phi,x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{l}|\phi,x)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|\phi,x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|\phi,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|\phi,x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|\phi,x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w},\phi|x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w},\phi|x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(53)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l},\phi|x)+\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l},\phi|x)+\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w},\phi|x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l},\phi|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w},\phi|x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l},\phi|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">where the <math id="A3.SS1.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\phi|x)</annotation></semantics></math> terms cancel, resulting in no direct <math id="A3.SS1.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> gradient contribution.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A3.SS1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(54)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{w}|x)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{l}|x)}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{w}|x)}-\log\frac{\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(f_{l}|x)}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, expanding the marginal probabilities using the law of total probability <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jeffreys, 1998</a>)</cite>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(55)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\theta}(f|x)=\sum_{\phi^{\prime}}\pi_{\theta}(f,\phi^{\prime}|x)=\sum_{\phi^{\prime}}\pi_{\theta}(f|\phi^{\prime},x)\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\theta}(f|x)=\sum_{\phi^{\prime}}\pi_{\theta}(f,\phi^{\prime}|x)=\sum_{\phi^{\prime}}\pi_{\theta}(f|\phi^{\prime},x)\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">We then take the gradient to derive:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p30" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(56)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(f|x)}{\pi_{\theta}(f|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(f|x)}{\pi_{\theta}(f|x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\pi_{\theta}(f|x)}\nabla_{\theta}\sum_{\phi^{\prime}}\pi_{\theta}(f|\phi^{\prime},x)\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\pi_{\theta}(f|x)}\nabla_{\theta}\sum_{\phi^{\prime}}\pi_{\theta}(f|\phi^{\prime},x)\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\pi_{\theta}(f|x)}\sum_{\phi^{\prime}}\Big[\pi_{\theta}(f|\phi^{\prime},x)\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\pi_{\theta}(f|x)}\sum_{\phi^{\prime}}\Big[\pi_{\theta}(f|\phi^{\prime},x)\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(57)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(f|\phi^{\prime},x)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(f|\phi^{\prime},x)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">Unlike in the first term, the gradients <math id="A3.SS1.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)</annotation></semantics></math> do </span><span id="A3.SS1.p31.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">not</span><span id="A3.SS1.p31.1.3" class="ltx_text"> cancel out. This means <math id="A3.SS1.p31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> explicitly captures gradients of the frictive state distribution.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining both terms in the loss gradient, we can represent the gradient expression for <math id="A3.SS1.p32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{FAAF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>FAAF</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{FAAF}}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p33" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(58)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E58.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\mu}}\left[-2\delta^{\prime}\cdot(\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R+\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\mu}}\left[-2\delta^{\prime}\cdot(\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R+\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\mu}}\Bigg[-2\delta^{\prime}\cdot\Bigg(\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w},\phi|x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l},\phi|x)}_{\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}_{\mu}}\Bigg[-2\delta^{\prime}\cdot\Bigg(\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w},\phi|x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l},\phi|x)}_{\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|x)}_{\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime}}\Bigg)\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\underbrace{\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{w}|x)-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f_{l}|x)}_{\nabla_{\theta}\Delta R^{\prime}}\Bigg)\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p34.1.1" class="ltx_text">Where <math id="A3.SS1.p34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{\prime}=\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{\prime}=\frac{1}{2\beta}-(\Delta R+\Delta R^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and the gradient of the marginal terms <math id="A3.SS1.p34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(f|x)</annotation></semantics></math> includes direct contributions from the frictive state <math id="A3.SS1.p34.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> through the weighted sum of <math id="A3.SS1.p34.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}(\phi^{\prime}|x)</annotation></semantics></math> terms. The second component specifically incorporates gradients of <math id="A3.SS1.p34.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\phi|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\phi|x)</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing the model to learn improved frictive state representations through direct gradient feedback, unlike the standard loss where these contributions vanish. Intuitively, including the <math id="A3.SS1.p34.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> form of the implicit reward margin in <math id="A3.SS1.p34.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{FAAF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>FAAF</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{FAAF}}</annotation></semantics></math> reflects a "fall-back" or "picking-up-the-slack" option during training that helps push the model toward the target preference gap <math id="A3.SS1.p34.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2\beta</annotation></semantics></math>—addressing certain failure modes in implicit-reward estimation. The preference gap can of course be data-dependent and can be picked optimally during model validation. But the idea of fallback options to avoid such failure modes has been found to be empirically viable, similar to methods like SMAUG <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib103" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pal et al., 2024</a>)</cite> which penalizes the model to retain a fixed-margin of implicit rewards. Therefore, in training the <span id="A3.SS1.p34.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">intervention agent</span> with <math id="A3.SS1.p34.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{FAAF}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>FAAF</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{FAAF}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the model improves its understanding of </span><span id="A3.SS1.p34.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">what</span><span id="A3.SS1.p34.1.3" class="ltx_text"> makes a viable frictive state, rather than just learning how to respond appropriately, given a frictive state.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p35" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p35.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Friction Agent Training Algorithm</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#alg1" title="In Appendix D Friction Agent Training Algorithm ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows the <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">friction agent</span> data generation and training algorithm. <a href="#A4.T3" title="In Appendix D Friction Agent Training Algorithm ‣ Collaborate, Deliberate, Evaluate: How LLM Alignment Affects Coordinated Multi-Agent Outcomes" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows the personality facets that were ascribed to different roleplay participants by <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Preference Data Generation and Training <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">friction agent</span> </figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
          Oracle agent <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>O</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, Collaborator agent <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>C</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, Bootstrap dialogues <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{d_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{d_{i}\}_{i=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, Personality-facet combinations <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, Max turns <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, Reference model (SFT) <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each dialogue <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
            Assign personality-facet combinations <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\sim\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\sim\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> to collaborators in <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\leftarrow d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\leftarrow d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize roleplay with bootstrap dialogue
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
